# whole-host record H4/W8/unenforced, from H4/W2
templates
T:call-context-manager-cm-3f216d510335 = Context Manager: [CM] Recall memory L#-#.
T:call-context-manager-system-7390a400c953 = Context Manager: System: You will soon form a new memory, get ready. The messages that follow are the slice of recent experience you are about to compress. After them, write the memory in your own voice.
T:call-context-manager-write-7f24f266d392 = Context Manager: Write the memory of events since the most recent memory system notification. Speak in the first person from your own perspective. Preserve concrete details — file paths, exact values, decisions, unresolved questions, the user's active asks. Target ~# tokens. Output only the memory body — no preamble, no section headers unless they help preservation, no meta-commentary about summarizing. Memorize only what actually happened in that slice: if it holds little beyond routine system traffic (heartbeats, empty turns, failure notices), a short memory saying so is correct — do not pad it by re-narrating events you already remember from earlier as if they had just happened again.
T:call-empty-ad1af52e2872 = 
  
  ---
  
  
T:call-routing-your-plain-d71d86cf6da8 = [routing] Your plain speech now lands in chat. Other channels need an explicit send tool.
T:call-the-local-time-1222d23a37ca = The local time at the start of this session is #-#-#T#:#:#.#+#:# [UTC].
T:call-user-clock-monday-c5cea0da131c = user: Clock: Monday #-#-#, #:# UTC
T:call-user-delivered-plain-c3f08a222233 = user: [delivered] plain speech → chat
T:subconscious-skip-reply-aebed2d843b9 = skip_reply {}
